//! The tables of the tests of the RSA functions (generated by `port_helpers/gen_rsa_tests.py`):
//! the keys, and what Warp 10 3.5.0 (BouncyCastle) answers to the scripts that use them. The
//! blocks of PKCS#1 and PSS that its answers are about are built by that script with integers,
//! apart from the code of the crate. A key is written `@PUBn` or `@PRIVn` in a script, `n` being
//! its size in bits.

